WEBVTT

00:00:57.845 --> 00:01:00.306
Becoming a theater
practitioner in Palestine

00:01:00.306 --> 00:01:03.518
is like conjuring water in the desert.

00:01:03.559 --> 00:01:05.394
We don't have the infrastructure,

00:01:05.436 --> 00:01:08.314
we don't have the big
artistic institutions.

00:01:08.356 --> 00:01:10.900
What we do have is a need

00:01:10.942 --> 00:01:13.528
and something to say
about the world we live in.

00:01:13.528 --> 00:01:17.907
Taking my shows to communities
and refugee camps in Palestine,

00:01:17.949 --> 00:01:22.578
I was always struck
by the immediacy of the encounter

00:01:22.620 --> 00:01:25.540
and that became a very powerful
experience for me.

00:01:25.957 --> 00:01:29.544
In 2015, at the height
of the refugee crisis,

00:01:29.585 --> 00:01:33.506
when hundreds of thousands of people
were walking across Europe,